; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; The owner's session at CART.9's third hand test, 2026-10-21, and a stand-in after it (decisions 14 and 26), so that
; the page's hand, the block hand-naught, holds a replay of the game and of the bench. Frames 1 to 45 are the owner's,
; as the owner's page recorded them: the load's act on the Lesson; on I NON the switch toggled by Space twice, set by
; 1 and 0, clicked twice, NON written from NON-ET and passed, and N; on II ET, VEL written where ET is due and the test
; stopping at input 2, then ET by NON of NON-ET, passed at its least known. Since CART.9's short slice of 2026-10-24
; those rows play against the cartridge as it stands, each act in the frames it took. Then a stand-in written by the
; engine's own steps in the form the host's recorder writes, each act's Input rows those that differ from the ones last
; logged, the engine releasing a press and a command after each: the levels III to IX of the engine's scripted
; session, III's input emptied by Delete, its error named before T and where the test stops, R, and a pass; IV's AUT
; with a gate outside the set, VEL times a number written as a text, which is no gate, one star; V at its least known;
; VI at the textbook's three gates, two stars; VII with two gates idle and outside the set, one star, which their
; Delete moves not until T again, three; VIII at its least known; and IX's four whole sums, a carry rippling, its 512
; inputs in 514 frames. Then the clocked levels of CART.9's fourth slice: X's flip-flop, a wire, its d set and C ticked,
; q a tick behind, G at rest; a gate that toggles q, G spending its two states; and the wire again; XI's bit held in one
; ELIGE, its flip-flop set by hand and its test forgotten by R; XII's four; XIII's counter, inc on and G, which never
; rests, its 16 ticks; XIV's reckoning, all 1,024 inputs; and XV's machine, half its gates failing T at an input its word
; stands on, C and R, the rest of them, its 2,048 inputs, G running the ROM's 3 x 5 to 15, a line rewritten, a word none
; of the five, and G again, 3 x 7 in four bits. Then the bench's 38 switches, each written in the drawer's edit row, its
; tab chosen at the first: the adder's a to all ones and its carry-in, 65,535 + 1 rippling through all sixteen bits; the
; multiplier's 255 x 255 = 65,025; and the low bits turned back, 254 x 127 = 32,258. Then I's switch written over,
; which the test no longer drives, so that it stops at input 1, and says so. And last, since CART.9's fifth slice, III's
; room given a gate outside the set that divides by zero, its verdict naming the #DIV/0!, and the cell emptied by
; Delete, the pass's words again. Every frame of the game is held to the hand
; where an act, a test, a clock or a person's row could move it, and one in 64 whole: the gates, the boards, the words,
; the Lab, the ROM, the Gates sheet and the Camera's sheet. Its golden is the Bench's record at its end.
(replay "naught" (spec 6) (cartridge "F1E3EB541E1F0E5B2F52B773ABC11809146848A3DFBBAEBC48168C33AD095B9F") (seed 1))
